IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Date helpers shared by the modules of the Regulations.
-- YMD is missing from the stable prelude, so this module defines it once; every
-- other module reaches it through IMPORT `pip-dates`.

§ `Date helpers`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

-- The period of N weeks beginning with a day: its last day.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the weeks beginning with` `the first day` `for` `the number of weeks` MEANS
    `the first day` PLUS ((`the number of weeks` TIMES 7) MINUS 1)

-- (daydate already defines `the day after` a date; `the day before` is written d MINUS 1.)

-- The first day of the period of N months ending with a date: the day after the
-- corresponding date N months earlier (add months clamps to the last day of a
-- shorter month; see the fork register of NOTES.md, month-end dates).
GIVEN `the last day` IS A DATE
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the months ending with` `the last day` `for` `the number of months` MEANS
    (`add months` `the last day` (0 MINUS `the number of months`)) PLUS 1

-- The last day of the period of N months beginning with a date: the day before the
-- corresponding date N months later.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the months beginning with` `the first day` `for` `the number of months` MEANS
    (`add months` `the first day` `the number of months`) MINUS 1
